challenges:
Our biggest challenges right now are;
1.Manufacturing operational capacity; Presently we operate at a limited fertilizers output capacity of 1.9 tonnes quarterly, limiting our reach to more small holder farmers in Nigeria.
2. Certification: Our product requires additional certifications to allow us access more market and scale our reach.

fundUsage:
The ₦5M grant will be allocated across: - backend hardening (₦1.5M) to ensure infrastructure can handle scale before marketing spend drives new users; 
- API, infrastructure, and domain costs (₦800K) covering DeepSeek, Supabase premium tier, Google Books API, and a custom domain; 
- marketing and distribution (₦1.7M) to solve the primary challenge of reach; 
- a part-time community moderator (₦500K) to support the most-requested feature from beta feedback; 
- and mobile/PWA polish (₦500K) to strengthen the Add-to-Home-Screen experience as a faster, cheaper path than native app development.
